    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579-a4">

                <pb facs="0706" n="646" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg646"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Customs, Canada</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Victoria, British
                                Columbia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May 28,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hardie</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Acting Deputy Minister of Marine, etc., Ottawa</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reverting to my letter of the 9th instant,
                    in answer to yours of the 22d ultimo, re schooners <hi rendition="#italic">Sea
                        Lion</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">C. E. Fox</hi>, I find in examining
                    the copy that an unaccountable error was made in giving the catch of the
                    schooner <hi rendition="#italic">Diana</hi>, formerly the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sea Lion</hi>, on the twenty-second line, by giving the
                    Copper Island catch as 43 instead of 433 the total, however, being correct. The
                    particulars should have been as follows: Japanese coast catch, 1,961; Copper
                    Island catch, 433; total, 2,394.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. R. Milne</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Collector.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
